From 3ba0f711642a888aec92a611a3f3b2211157ff89 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] usage-ring: avoid unsupported Android installation-id lock

Android app-private filesystems can reject the desktop advisory file lock after
creating an empty installation_id file. Keep the upstream resolver everywhere
else, while Android uses an atomically replaced UUID under the already
process-serialized in-process RuntimeController startup path.

--- a/codex-rs/app-server/src/in_process.rs
+++ b/codex-rs/app-server/src/in_process.rs
@@ -82,6 +82,7 @@ use codex_config::LoaderOverrides;
 use codex_config::ThreadConfigLoader;
 use codex_core::check_execpolicy_for_warnings;
